{
    "background_story": "Gustavo was a brilliant but eccentric scientist who spent most of his life studying the mysteries of quantum physics. His intense focus and obsessive nature often left him jittering with excitement, as if the very atoms in his body were vibrating with anticipation. As he worked tirelessly in his laboratory, Gustavo's hands would shake and his eyes would dart back and forth, as if racing to keep up with the rapid-fire thoughts in his mind. His colleagues often joked that his jittering was a sign of genius at work, and they weren't far off. Gustavo's groundbreaking research led to a major breakthrough in energy production, earning him international acclaim and a reputation as a true visionary.",
